# passc gold set — Proiectarea si Arhitectura Sistemelor Software Complexe.
# Questions drawn from `subiecte.md` (the course's own review-question sheet, itself
# indexed) plus hand-written items. `expected` always points at the LECTURE slides that
# answer the question, never at subiecte.md — groundly/eval/gold.py rejects that, because
# it would score retrieving the question rather than the material answering it.
#
# 3 of the 44 review questions are deliberately NOT included: the Data Binding group
# ("What is Data Binding?", "Data Binding related to protobuf in gRPC", "Data Binding vs
# ORM"). The term appears nowhere in the decks except the course-topics list on
# Intro.pdf p10 — a labelled question whose answer is not in the corpus measures the
# corpus, not the arm, and drops every arm's hit rate by the same amount.
#
# Labels are (filename, page) and resolve against the live store at run time. Every page
# named below carries at least one extracted chunk: several slides are diagram-only and
# produce none (RPC.pdf p22-23 hold the Remote Proxy class diagram and extract nothing),
# so those questions are labelled on the pages that state the same content in text.
#
# Corpus note: the publish-subscribe material ships as two decks
# (PublishSubscribe-Greenrobot.pdf, PublishSubscribe-RabbitMQ.pdf), and DAO.pdf plus
# ObserverPatternReview.pdf cover topics the review sheet asks about directly.

